ponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-33b11ae2-1485-4b88-93c0-e28bed2e1f98"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolving self-organizing simulated plant-inspired robots","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382025","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we discuss a new type of robot for underwater hull cleaning on ships with non-magnetic hulls. This robot is based on the concept that cleaning hulls regularly, without waiting to take them out of the water, will improve the efficiency of the ships and will permit a reduction in the use of the chemicals that are usually employed to prevent the growth of marine life on the hull and which are generally harmful to the environment. The robot described in this paper is an underactuated morphologically adapted robot that through an appropriate morphology and making use of the forces and constraints of the environment solves the most difficult problems that arise when moving along hulls. Some of these are changing planes, negotiating appendices, avoiding portholes, passing corners, and other elements. This greatly simplifies the control mechanisms that are required for its operation making it an ideal candidate for completely autonomous operation. A description of the design of the robot as well as a series of examples of its operation are provided.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Souto, Daniel","Faina, Andres","López-Peña, Fernando","Duro, Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384754"],"event":{"end":"2015-09-26","place":"Warsaw, pl","start":"2015-09-24","title":"The 8th IEEE International Conference on Intelligent Data Acquisition and Advanced Computing Systems","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universidade da Coruña"],"keyword":["Robotics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"morphologically intelligent underactuated robot for underwater hull cleaning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84957546683","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384754","identifier":[{"id":"84957546683","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-eca73580-6842-47b1-bae2-2fc460ece22c"],"keyword":["Robotics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B5771415C0728AF5D04FDAF6B966803E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"es","key":"universidade da coruña","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universidade da Coruña","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"soutopau","last":"Souto","name":"Souto, Daniel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fernando","key":"lópezpeñapau","last":"López-Peña","name":"López-Peña, Fernando","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard","key":"duropau","last":"Duro","name":"Duro, Richard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/idaacs.2015.7341430","isbn":["9781467383592"],"pages":"879-886","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the IEEE 8th International Conference on Intelligent Data Acquisition and Advanced Computing Systems: Technology and Applications (IDAACS), 2015","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84957546683"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-eca73580-6842-47b1-bae2-2fc460ece22c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Morphologically intelligent underactuated robot for underwater hull cleaning","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384754","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Besides the life-as-it-could-be driver of artificial life research there is also the concept of extending natural life by creating hybrids or mixed societies that are built from natural and artificial components. In this paper we motivate and present the research program of the project flora robotica. Our objective is to develop and to investigate closely linked symbiotic relationships between robots and natural plants and to explore the potentials of a plant-robot society able to produce architectural artifacts and living spaces. These robot-plant bio-hybrids create synergies that allow for new functions of plants and robots. They also create novel design opportunities for an architecture that fuses the design and construction phase. The bio-hybrid is an example of mixed societies between ‘hard artificial and ‘wet natural life, which enables an interaction between natural and artificial ecologies. They form an embodied, self-organizing, and distributed cognitive system which is supposed to grow and develop over long periods of time resulting in the creation of meaningful architectural structures. A key idea is to assign equal roles to robots and plants in order to create a highly integrated, symbiotic system. Besides the gain of knowledge, this project has the objective to create a bio-hybrid system with a defined function and application – growing architectural artifacts.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Hamann, Heiko","Wahby, Mostafa","Schmickl, Thomas","Zahadat, Payam","Hofstadler, Daniel","Støy, Kasper","Risi, Sebastian","Faina, Andres","Veenstra, Frank","Kernbach, Serge","Kuksin, Igor","Kernbach, Olga","Ayers, Phil","Wojtaszek, Przemyslaw"],"cuid":["S02-089.67-012432"],"event":{"acronym":"IEEE SSCI","end":"2015-12-10","place":"Cape Town, za","start":"2015-12-07","title":"2015 IEEE Symposium on Artifical Life","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany","Poland"],"glorg":["Adam Mickiewicz University","All Global Affiliations","Cybertronica UG (Haftungsbeschrankt)","University of Graz","University of Paderborn"],"keyword":["Architecture","Artificial Life","Bio hybrid","Bio hybrid systems","Plants","Robots","Self organizing systems","architectural artifacts","plant robot symbiosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flora robotica mixed societies of symbiotic robot plant bio hybrids","src":["arkc","itu"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/SSCI.2015.158","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.67-012432","identifier":[{"id":"84964937762","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["arkc-8a5ce1d1-e2e0-4c7d-9e51-2001d8744f9a","itu-4181dddd-1be3-4361-8109-ca1419e73d88"],"keyword":["Architecture","Bio-hybrid","No","Plants","Robots","architectural artifacts","artificial life","bio-hybrid systems","plant-robot symbiosis","self-organizing systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AB54DC9B986B7E29B1E706A371F1092E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/80993764/IEEE_ALIFE_2015.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/SSCI.2015.158","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of paderborn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Paderborn","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"university of graz","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Graz","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"it