rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Phil","key":"ayersphilpau","last":"Ayers","name":"Ayers, Phil","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ssci.2015.158","isbn":["9781479975600"],"pages":"1102-1109","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Computational Intelligence, 2015 IEEE Symposium Series on"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84964937762"],"search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-8a5ce1d1-e2e0-4c7d-9e51-2001d8744f9a","itu-4181dddd-1be3-4361-8109-ca1419e73d88"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"Flora Robotica – Mixed Societies of Symbiotic Robot-Plant Bio-Hybrids","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.67-012432","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"This chapter is concerned with proposing ways to make feasible the use of robots in many sectors characterized by dynamic and unstructured environments. In particular, we are interested in addressing the problem through a new approach, based on modular robotics, to allow the fast deployment of robotsto solve specific tasks. A series of authors have previously proposed modular architectures, albeit mostly in laboratory settings. For this reason, their designs were usually more focused on what could be built instead of what was necessary for industrial operations. The approach presented here addresses the problem the other way around. In this line, we start by defining the industrial settings the architecture is aimed at and then extract the main features that would be required from a modular robotic architecture to operate successfully in this context. Finally, a particular heterogeneous modular robotic architecture is designed from these requirements and a laboratory implementation of it is built in order to test its capabilities and show its versatility using a set of different configurations including manipulators, climbers and walkers.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Faina, Andres","Orjales, Felix","Souto, Daniel","Bellas, Francisco","Duro, Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383150"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universidade da Coruña"],"keyword":["Collaborative automation","Control and Intelligence","Robots","Sensing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a modular architecture for developing robots for industrial applications","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85071759026","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383150","identifier":[{"id":"85071759026","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8088bcfa-c179-4d3b-8ecd-868aa210de75"],"keyword":["Collaborative automation","Control and Intelligence","Robots","Sensing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-A6B29AA2F93B118A304913ADF53911CE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"universidade da coruña","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universidade da Coruña","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Felix","key":"orjalespau","last":"Orjales","name":"Orjales, Felix","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"soutopau","last":"Souto","name":"Souto, Daniel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Francisco","key":"bellaspau","last":"Bellas","name":"Bellas, Francisco","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard","key":"duropau","last":"Duro","name":"Duro, Richard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788793237032"],"publisher":"River Publishers","status":"p","title":"Advances in Intelligent Robotics and Collaborative Automation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85071759026"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8088bcfa-c179-4d3b-8ecd-868aa210de75"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Modular Architecture for Developing Robots for Industrial Applications","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383150","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we aim to develop a controller that allows a robot to traverse an structured environment. The approach we use is to decompose the environment into simple sub-environments that we use as basis for evolving the controller. Specifically, we decompose a narrow corridor environment into four different sub-environments and evolve controllers that generalize to traverse two larger environments composed of the sub-environments. We also study two strategies for presenting the sub-environments to the evolutionary algorithm: all sub-environments at the same time and in sequence. Results show that by using a sequence the evolutionary algorithm can find a controller that performs well in all sub-environments more consistently than when presenting all sub-environments together. We conclude that environment decomposition is an useful approach for evolving controllers for structured environments and that the order in which the decomposed sub-environments are presented in sequence impacts the performance of the evolutionary algorithm.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Moreno, Rodrigo","Faina, Andres","Støy, Kasper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382200"],"event":{"acronym":"EvoApplications","end":"2015-04-10","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2015-04-08","title":"Evolutionary Computation in Robotics","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","OECD"],"country":["Colombia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National University of Colombia"],"keyword":["Environment decomposition","Evolutionary Robotics","Sequential evolution"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolving robot controllers for structured environments through environment decomposition","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81825184/Evostar2015MFS.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382200","identifier":[{"id":"84925862610","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3ef876ab-33f2-4831-9df7-36273ad39522"],"keyword":["Environment decomposition","Evolutionary robotics","Sequential evolution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D9CBA7B3137818572AF65AFCBA3EBE37"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81825184/Evostar2015MFS.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"co","key":"national university of colombia","loc":["Colombia","America, South","OECD"],"name":"National University of Colombia","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rodrigo","key":"morenopau","last":"Moreno","name":"Moreno, Rodrigo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"faiñapau","last":"Faiña","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","name_org":"Faiña, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"2a9c0934-98ca-4101-b829-b88d77f6487e","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9783319165493"],"isbn":["9783319165486"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"795-806","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"18th European Conference, EvoApplications 2015, Copenhagen, Denmark, April 8-10, 2015, Proceedings","title":"Applications of Evolutionary Computation","volume":"9028"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84925862610"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3ef876ab-33f2-4831-9df7-36273ad39522"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolving Robot Controllers for Structured Environments Through Environment Decomposition","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382200","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"This paper proposes the use of a modular robotic architecture in order to produce feasible robots through evolution. To this end, the main requirements the architecture must fulfill are analyzed and a top-down methodology is employed to obtain the different types of modules that make it up. Specifically, the problem of how to increase the evolvability or evolution friendliness of the system is addressed by considering a heterogeneous modular architecture with a large number of connection faces per module. Afterwards, a prototypical implementation of these modules with the required features is described and different experiments provide an indication of how versatile the architecture is for evolving robot morphologies and control for specific tasks and how easy it is to build them.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Faina, Andres","Bellas, Francisco","Orjales, Felix","Souto, Daniel","Duro, Richard J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382310"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universidade da Coruña"],"keyword":["Evolutionary Robotics","Evolutionary design","Modular Robots"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an evolution friendly modular architecture to produce feasible robots","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.robot.2014.07.014","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382310","identifier":[{"id":"84906113743","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-46268fbb-aae9-4fdc-a8f4-78aa85621e5d"],"keyword":["Evolutionary design","Evolutionary robotics","Modular Robots"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6D92C6989C8E65D768058A155CCAED83"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S092188901400147X","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/79272668/2015_faina_RAS.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81825167/faina2015an_evolution_friendly_modular_architecture_to_produce_feasible_robots_postreview.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.robot.2014.07.014","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"universidade da coruña","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universidade da Coruña","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Francisco","key":"bellaspau","last":"Bellas","name":"Bellas, Francisco","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Felix","key":"orjalespau","last":"Orjales","name":"Orjales, Felix","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"soutopau","last":"Souto","name":"Souto, Daniel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard J.","key":"duropau","last":"Duro","name":"Duro, Richard J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.robot.2014.07.014","issn":["09218890","1872793X"],"issn_org":["09218890"],"issue":"1","journal":"Robotics and Autonomous Systems","pages":"195","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Robotics and Autonomous Systems","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85027949955"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-46268fbb-aae9-4fdc-a8f4-78aa85621e5d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An evolution friendly modular architecture to produce feasible robots","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382310","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The EVOBLISS project combines scientific approaches from robotics, artificial intelligence, chemistry, and microbiology and aims to capitalize on the state of the art in these disparate disciplines and combine them together into a coherent project to produce i) a generally useful, expandable and customizable technical platform for the artificial evolution of new materials and applications based on a real-time feedback robotic workstation and ii) a specific improved technology, namely a microbial fuel cell, that incorporates natural as well as artificial macro-, micro-, and nanoscale elements for improved function. Scientifically, we will investigate the possibility of optimizing artificial chemical life, microbial ecosystems, and nanoparticles and their physiochemical, dynamic environments using robot facilitated, artificial evolution. This paper deals with the first goal of the EVOBLISS project, to produce a useful, expandable and customizable technical platform for the artificial evolution of new materials and applications. Specifically, the objective of this paper is to define the capabilities of our liquid handling robot, called EvoBot. This robot will be a mature and robust version of the SplotBot robot which was used to show the feasibility of this approach [1]. This robot was able to perform proof of concept experiments, but was too fragile to conduct systematic scientific experiments in artificial chemical life. Furthermore, the EvoBot robot will increase the features of the SplotBot robot in order to make new types of experiments. Proceeding, the capabilities of the EvoBots are presented based on prerequisites for mature and robust functionality, and also features requested by partners.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Faina, Andres","Nejatimoharrami, Farzad","Støy, Kasper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382578"],"event":{"end":"2014-08-30","place":"New York, us","start":"2014-08-30","title":"Exploiting synergies between biology and artificial life technologies: tools, possibilities, and examples","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Liquid handling","Robotics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards evobot a liquid handling robot able to automatize and optimize experiments based on real time feedback","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/76542200/ALIFE14_evobot.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382578","ids":["itu-584b4e9b-e442-40db-b0fe-15de3ea843b5"],"keyword":["Liquid handling","Robotics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-525DFDFA72F908D490D5CADB52484388"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/76542200/ALIFE14_evobot.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Farzad","key":"nejatimoharramipau","last":"Nejatimoharrami","name":"Nejatimoharrami, Farzad","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"2a9c0934-98ca-4101-b829-b88d77f6487e","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-584b4e9b-e442-40db-b0fe-15de3ea843b5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards EvoBot: A liquid-handling robot able to automatize and optimize experiments based on real-time feedback","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382578","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This paper provides a brief description of the robots obtained using the evolutionary design system called EDHMoR (Evolutionary Designer of Heterogeneous Modular Robots) that are displayed in the corresponding video [1]. This system is based on the coevolution of morphology and control with the main objective of obtaining feasible and manufacturable robots. To this end, a modular architecture has been defined and implemented [2], which faces real hardware issues and promotes the evolvability of the robotic structures by considering heterogeneous modules with a large number of connection faces per module. These modules constitute the building blocks the EDHMoR system uses to design the robots. Moreover, an evaluation methodology is proposed as a key element of EDMHoR, which is based on modifications in the environment that can produce more useful and realistic robots without limiting the search space. The video shows some of the resulting robots for two different tasks, painting a surface and walking, and the influence of these modifications. Finally, some real tests of these morphologies are presented.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Faina, Andres","Souto, Daniel","Orjales, Félix","Bellas, Francisco","Duro, Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383438"],"event":{"end":"2014-07-16","place":"Vancouver, ca","start":"2014-07-12","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universidade da Coruña"],"keyword":["Evolutionary Robotics","Robotics","Virtual creatures"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from virtual creatures to feasible robots","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/76492677/2014_gecco_virtual_creatures_contest_afaina_et_al_final.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-383438","ids":["itu-93a1dd0f-9534-4e27-aea6-9849887945f0"],"keyword":["Evolutionary robotics","Robotics","Virtual creatures"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2D7AD3CB8F5FA7C7C94B4C2293A760E4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/76492678/Virtual_Creatures.mp4","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/76492677/2014_gecco_virtual_creatures_contest_afaina_et_al_final.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"universidade da coruña","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universidade da Coruña","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"soutopau","last":"Souto","name":"Souto, Daniel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Félix","key":"orjalespau","last":"Orjales","name":"Orjales, Félix","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Francisco","key":"bellaspau","last":"Bellas","name":"Bellas, Francisco","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard","key":"duropau","last":"Duro","name":"Duro, Richard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-93a1dd0f-9534-4e27-aea6-9849887945f0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"From Virtual Creatures to Feasible Robots","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383438","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
